# Forms: React Hook Form + Zod

Every user-editable `<form>` validates with **React Hook Form** + **Zod** (`zodResolver`). Do not use ad-hoc `useState` + `onSubmit` checks for field validation.

```tsx
// ❌ BAD — manual field state / HTML-only required
const [email, setEmail] = useState("");
<form onSubmit={(e) => { e.preventDefault(); /* … */ }}>

// ✅ GOOD
const schema = useMemo(() => loginSchema({ … }), [te]);
const { register, handleSubmit, formState: { errors } } = useForm({
  resolver: zodResolver(schema),
  defaultValues: { email: "", password: "" },
});
<form onSubmit={handleSubmit(onSubmit)}>
  <Input {...register("email")} />
  {errors.email?.message ? <p>{errors.email.message}</p> : null}
```

## Conventions

- Schemas live in `apps/<app>/lib/validation/<feature>.ts` (factory with i18n messages).
- Wire fields with `register` or `Controller`; show `errors.<field>.message` via i18n strings.
- Keep API / mutation errors separate from field errors (`AuthAlert` / toast).
- Shared inputs that accept `register()` must `forwardRef` to the native control (`AuthField`, `AuthPasswordField`, `Input`).

Do not invent another form library. Full text: `docs/architecture/frontend-feature-playbook.md`.
